* Calculate Runner Status: Sets RUNNER STATUS based on race progress.
*   When to use:    During the race to update runner status for LPT, or after recalculating.
*   How to use:     Double-click to recalculate all runner statuses.
*   Note:           Requires GunStart, ChipStart, and FINISH events. Sets:
*                   COMPLETE     - FINISH is not empty
*                   IN_PROGRESS  - any mat read (ChipStart or a split), FINISH empty
*                   STARTING     - no mat read anywhere yet
*   Depends on:     Events must be written to DB fields first (Events2DB.rsm).

* Step 1: Clear runner status and event database fields
clear-f.rsm         "RUNNER STATUS"
clear-f.rsm         CHIPSTART
clear-f.rsm         FINISH
clear-f.rsm         Split1k
clear-f.rsm         Split2k
clear-f.rsm         Split5k
clear-f.rsm         Split8k
clear-f.rsm         Split10k
clear-f.rsm         Split18k

* Step 2: Write events to database fields
Events2DB.rsm

* Step 3: Set status for finishers
set-status-complete.rsm

* Step 4: Set status for in-progress runners -- one call per on-course field.
* A runner who missed the start mat but hit a split still counts as on course.
set-status-inprogress.rsm   CHIPSTART
set-status-inprogress.rsm   Split1k
set-status-inprogress.rsm   Split2k
set-status-inprogress.rsm   Split5k
set-status-inprogress.rsm   Split8k
set-status-inprogress.rsm   Split10k
set-status-inprogress.rsm   Split18k

* Step 5: Everyone left has no time anywhere -- still on the start list
set-status-starting.rsm
